  "articleBody": "Okay, so you've been in a car accident and your vehicle is damaged – that's a tough spot to be in, but you've got options. First things first, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if there are any injuries. Once the immediate danger is handled, you'll need to think about your car. Documenting everything at the scene is super important, like taking photos of the damage, the other vehicles involved, and the surroundings. Get the other driver's information and any witness contacts. Then, you'll want to report the accident to your insurance company. This is where things can get tricky, especially when dealing with the other driver's insurance or if liability is disputed. They might try to undervalue your damages or deny your claim outright. If you're feeling overwhelmed or like you're not getting a fair shake, that's a good time to get professional help. An attorney like Angelo Reyes, who understands property damage recovery, can step in to protect your interests, negotiate with insurers, and make sure you're pursuing the full compensation you deserve for repairs or replacement. Don't go it alone if the process feels like too much.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}